.TH QFW-SERVICE-PLANE 7 "August 2026" "QFw 0.1.0" "QFw Concepts"
.SH NAME
qfw-service-plane \- QFw service ownership and runtime-state model
.SH OVERVIEW
A service plane groups the persistent processes that provide QPM discovery and
execution. It may contain a DEFw directory service, an optional PRTE DVM, and
one QPM service.
.PP
The administrator or application selects authoritative YAML configuration.
.BR qfw-dir-svc (1)
manages one directory instance, while
.BR qfw-qpm-svc (1)
manages one QPM and its optional DVM. The combined
.BR qfw-service-plane (1)
interface remains available for compatibility. Each command writes resolved
configuration as generated instance state.
.SH OWNERSHIP
A site directory and each site QPM are started independently by an
administrator or service manager. They may serve several independent
application jobs and their lifetime is independent of application teardown.
.PP
An application-owned plane is started inside an application allocation. Its
components carry application ownership and are stopped when that plane is
released.
.PP
The manager stops only components recorded as owned by its service-plane
instance. Attached or externally managed services remain outside its teardown
boundary.
.SH RUN DIRECTORY
Each directory or QPM manager has one explicit run directory. The path remains
stable for the lifetime of that instance. It contains generated state, client
connection settings, PID files, readiness records, and logs.
.PP
Multinode simulator deployments place this directory on storage visible at the
same pathname from every simulator node. PRTE writes its DVM URI there, and the
QPM reads that URI when launching simulator work.
.PP
Applications connecting to an existing site plane need the client connection
environment. They do not need the service-side DVM URI.
.SH LIFECYCLE
The generated state uses the lifecycle values
.BR starting ,
.BR ready ,
.BR degraded ,
.BR stopped ,
and
.BR error .
Readiness requires every configured component to have a valid readiness record
and, for PID-backed components, a live recorded process.
.PP
The foreground
.B run
operation supervises components and exits nonzero when an owned component
fails. SIGINT and SIGTERM trigger reverse-order shutdown.
.SH BACKEND TOPOLOGY
Remote IQM and fakeIQM service planes do not require PRTE. Simulator services
such as NWQ-Sim and TNQVM may use a DVM across assigned simulator nodes. The
runtime configuration selects PRTE explicitly through
.BR start-prte .
.SH STATE AND CONFIGURATION
YAML files remain authoritative user and administrator configuration. The
.I state/service-plane.json
file records the resolved instance and observed runtime state. Operators do not
edit this generated file.
.PP
Static configuration is referenced by path. Credential values are excluded
from generated client environment and service-plane state.
